# Tellme — environment variable reference.
# Two SEPARATE secret systems; do not mix them up (infrastructure.md risk register).

# ── Backend API (Cloudflare Worker) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev: copy these into backend/.dev.vars (gitignored), read by `wrangler dev`.
# Production: set via `wrangler secret put <NAME>` (encrypted, per-Worker). Do NOT commit.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<supabase-anon-public-key>   # anon key, NOT service_role
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-<...>                  # Claude task extraction (POST /transcribe)
# Transcription uses the Cloudflare Workers AI binding (wrangler.toml [ai]) — no key.

# Optional — real cross-user (IDOR) integration test in backend/test/idor.test.ts.
# Two CONFIRMED Supabase Auth users (create via Dashboard → Authentication → Users →
# "Add user", with "Auto Confirm User" checked). The test skips itself when unset.
# TEST_USER_A_EMAIL=idor-test-a@example.com
# TEST_USER_A_PASSWORD=<...>
# TEST_USER_B_EMAIL=idor-test-b@example.com
# TEST_USER_B_PASSWORD=<...>

# ── Mobile app (Expo / EAS) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build/runtime secrets are managed with `eas secret:create --name <NAME> --value <...>`,
# NOT with wrangler. (Public values can also go in app.json `extra`.)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://tellme-backend.konrad-matulewicz1.workers.dev
